(2204641, 298836, 31403, '<td valign="top">I think conceptually this is the best in the challenge - and photographically it''s very close too.  <br/> <br/>Great set up and really great thought went into this.  <br/> <br/>I understand being frustrated with the masses not seeing my vision - I''ve decided a check is better than a ribbon, and art directors and photo buyers giving defined "challenges" beats the vagueness here.  I could go on, PM me if you really care.  ;-)<br/> <br/>But you ARE a great photographer, and ARE a great artist - the tantrum alone tells me about the artist part!  :-)  (having thrown a few myself).<br/> <br/>So smile - yours is worthy of a gallery - something that I can''t say for any of the front page IMO.</td>', 'I think conceptually this is the best in the challenge - and photographically it''s very close too.   Great set up and really great thought went into this.   I understand being frustrated with the masses not seeing my vision - I''ve decided a check is better than a ribbon, and art directors and photo buyers giving defined "challenges" beats the vagueness here.  I could go on, PM me if you really care.  ;-) But you ARE a great photographer, and ARE a great artist - the tantrum alone tells me about the artist part!  :-)  (having thrown a few myself). So smile - yours is worthy of a gallery - something that I can''t say for any of the front page IMO.', '2006-03-06 14:35:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(2204705, 300783, 19708, '<td valign="top">As I expected - many didn''t see what I saw regarding to "Odd".<br/>Guess quality made up for the stretch into fitting the challenge.<br/>Study it for a little bit - the mirror imaging is uncanny.<br/>Gotta'' love a 6.0 though - Thanks!<br/></td>', 'As I expected - many didn''t see what I saw regarding to "Odd".Guess quality made up for the stretch into fitting the challenge.Study it for a little bit - the mirror imaging is uncanny.Gotta'' love a 6.0 though - Thanks!', '2006-03-06 14:55:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(2204766, 300623, 52034, '<td valign="top">I think it''s sad that so many people immediately see anyone with piercings as "odd." (Also, the female''s looks much too low for a ring. It should probably be a labret.)<br/> <br/>The photo was very technically well done though. Congratulations on winning!</td>', 'I think it''s sad that so many people immediately see anyone with piercings as "odd." (Also, the female''s looks much too low for a ring. It should probably be a labret.) The photo was very technically well done though. Congratulations on winning!', '2006-03-06 15:14:50.000000', NULL, 0),
